  "research_note": "THE WATER TOWER, built by T-3689 for the 1871 scene, from the Historic American Buildings Survey's measured drawings (1994) and P. B. Greene's stereograph of 1871. A base 43 feet square with an octagonal turret at each corner and a pointed doorway in each front, a 25-foot upper stage with four pinnacles and a stone gable on each face, then the octagonal shaft, 15 feet 6 inches across, to a battlemented cornice at about 154 feet, and the iron cupola and mast to 182 feet 6 inches. Joliet limestone, rock-faced, buff. It survived the fire.",
